# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Local verification artifacts
.verify/
.smoke/

# Packed tarballs
*.tgz

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# ⚠️ Never commit `.npmrc`.
#
# A developer's `~/.npmrc` often holds a plaintext publish token —
#
#     //registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=npm_…
#
# — and a project-level `.npmrc` is exactly where people put one when they need it. This repository
# is published publicly, so a single `git add -A` would put that token on the internet with **publish
# rights to the npm account**.
#
# It matters less than it used to, because `publish.yml` authenticates with OIDC and needs no token
# at all — there is deliberately no `NPM_TOKEN` anywhere in this repo. But a `.npmrc` can still be
# created by a tool, by an editor, or by hand, so the ignore rule stays.
.npmrc

# ⚠️ `lib/` is deliberately NOT here.
#
# In this package `lib/` is source code, not build output — there is no build step at all. It holds
# every module the plugin is made of, and `index.js` requires them.
#
# Adding `lib/` to this file would also, silently, remove it from the published tarball: npm's pack
# step consults `.gitignore` when a package has no `.npmignore` entry of its own, so a rule written
# to keep a local directory out of Git ends up deciding what users install. That is exactly how
# dsh-wechat once shipped a plugin with no entry point to load. See `.npmignore` for the other half
# of this.
